{"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/swift\/anyregexoutput\/reversed()"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"metadata":{"fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"reversed","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() -> ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:s18ReversedCollectionV","text":"ReversedCollection","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">","kind":"text"}],"symbolKind":"method","platforms":[{"deprecated":false,"name":"iOS","unavailable":false,"beta":false,"introducedAt":"8.0"},{"deprecated":false,"name":"iPadOS","unavailable":false,"beta":false,"introducedAt":"8.0"},{"deprecated":false,"name":"Mac Catalyst","unavailable":false,"beta":false,"introducedAt":"13.0"},{"deprecated":false,"name":"macOS","unavailable":false,"beta":false,"introducedAt":"10.10"},{"deprecated":false,"name":"tvOS","unavailable":false,"beta":false,"introducedAt":"9.0"},{"deprecated":false,"name":"visionOS","unavailable":false,"beta":false,"introducedAt":"1.0"},{"deprecated":false,"name":"watchOS","unavailable":false,"beta":false,"introducedAt":"2.0"}],"title":"reversed()","extendedModule":"Swift","externalID":"s:SKsE8reverseds18ReversedCollectionVyxGyF::SYNTHESIZED::s:17_StringProcessing14AnyRegexOutputV","modules":[{"name":"Swift","relatedModules":[]}],"roleHeading":"Instance Method","role":"symbol"},"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"reversed","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"ReversedCollection","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/ReversedCollection","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:s18ReversedCollectionV"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">","kind":"text"}]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"type":"heading","anchor":"discussion","text":"Discussion","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"You can reverse a collection without allocating new space for its","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"elements by calling this ","type":"text"},{"code":"reversed()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" method. A ","type":"text"},{"code":"ReversedCollection","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"instance wraps an underlying collection and provides access to its","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"elements in reverse order. This example prints the characters of a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"string in reverse order:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["let word = \"Backwards\"","for char in word.reversed() {","    print(char, terminator: \"\")","}","\/\/ Prints \"sdrawkcaB\""],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"If you need a reversed collection of the same type, you may be able to","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"use the collection’s sequence-based or collection-based initializer. For","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"example, to get the reversed version of a string, reverse its","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"characters and initialize a new ","type":"text"},{"code":"String","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" instance from the result.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["let reversedWord = String(word.reversed())","print(reversedWord)","\/\/ Prints \"sdrawkcaB\""],"type":"codeListing"},{"name":"Complexity","style":"note","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"O(1)"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"type":"aside"}],"kind":"content"}],"kind":"symbol","schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Returns a view presenting the elements of the collection in reverse"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"order."}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift","doc:\/